# .claude/ is tracked, because it *is* how this project works: the rules an implementer writes
# code against, the agent and skill definitions, the hooks that gate a run, and the templates
# every loop fills in. While the whole directory was ignored, none of it reached a
# worktree-isolated agent — the same failure that made the design docs unreadable until they
# moved to docs/. Three things under it stay out:
#
#   loops/               per-run state, plans and trajectories. Local to whoever ran the loop,
#                        regenerated every time, and of no use to anyone else's checkout.
#   worktrees/           agent worktrees — each one a near-full checkout of this repository.
#   settings.local.json  personal permission overrides, not shared configuration.
.claude/loops/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# docs-tmp/ is the private half of the documentation, and it holds three different kinds of
# thing — worth naming, because only the last one is a security boundary:
#   - operational runbooks that name real infrastructure: polar-e2e.md, DEPLOY.md and
#     WORKOS-PRODUCTION.md carry organization ids, the Supabase project ref and WorkOS ids;
#   - pricing-tiers.md, kept private by decision rather than by necessity — it carries Polar
#     product ids, which are not secrets (they appear in checkout URLs) but are per-environment
#     configuration nobody outside this project needs;
#   - PORTAL-ENV.md and supabase-pass.md, which hold live credentials.
#
# The design docs that used to live here — the architecture spec, the build plan, the research
# survey and the design system — are tracked under docs/ now, because AGENTS.md and several
# source comments cite them as the project's contract and a fresh clone did not have them.
docs-tmp/
supabase-pass.md

# Live credentials for the portal deploy — never commit (public repo).
PORTAL-ENV.md
